 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+Each entity has **queues** (persisted in `queues`). A queue belongs to one
+entity and has a `name`, a `slug` unique within the entity, an `is_active`
+flag (default true) and optional `labels_i18n` (JSON multilingual labels).
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single
+call**. Persisted attributes (`tickets`):
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code` — per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 zero-padded digits; beyond 999 it simply grows: `A1000`, `A1001`, …). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`. The next code is the last valid code + 1 by insertion order (not string order); deleted tickets do not reuse their number in the normal case and malformed legacy codes (anything not matching `A<digits>`) are skipped.
+- Priority (numeric, see below; `>= 0`, default `0`).
+- Issuance timestamp (`issued_at`, ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default), `printed`.
+- `status`: `waiting` (new tickets) or `called`; there is no cancelled status.
+- Call fields `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called).
+
+Rules:
+
+- **Issuance** (`App\Actions\IssueTicket`) rejects inactive queues. The queue state is re-read from the database inside the transaction (the queue row is locked), so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected and nothing is persisted. A negative priority is rejected, and issuance retries a few times on a concurrent `(queue_id, code)` collision.
+- **Write-once**: after issuance every ticket field is immutable except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (plus `updated_at`).
+- **Single call** (`Ticket::call()`): a waiting ticket can be called exactly once, recording `called_at` and the calling user. Only members of the ticket's entity may call; calling a non-waiting ticket fails. Selecting *which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is a separate concern.
 
 ### Priority
 
